            <chunk name="Object" index="11">
              <items count="3">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">a9af5ab1-4a15-4a44-bb7d-83d9e4688711</item>
                <item name="Lib" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">6b0b6c1e-3f0a-4c55-9a43-2f7d4c1f8a10</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Check Layers</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="5">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Checks layers you designed yourself. Give the points of each layer (one branch per layer, lowest first, or one spiral) and, if you have them, the layer heights. It builds the wall through your points and runs every check Clay Print does: layer height limits, layer contact, overhang, bead support and nozzle tilt at every point, and the structure (bond between the layers, every print stage, buckling) with the base on the bed under its own weight.
Faces that fail are grouped into areas: Issues says what is wrong and what to change, Issue Points and Issue Areas show where. Your layers are not changed or re-sliced, so change your definition and watch the issues go.</item>
                    <item name="Hidden" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">6b03d404-5c5b-498b-a162-c444d8ab0ca0</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Check Layers</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Check Layers</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="19">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
